-- Ruler: citing provision, line in the text file, words as printed, instrument as printed, provision as printed.
`other-instrument reference 001` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 1(e)", 33, "the Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982", "Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982", ""
`other-instrument reference 002` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 1(f)", 34, "the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", ""
`other-instrument reference 003` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 1(f)", 34, "the Sentencing Act 1991", "Sentencing Act 1991", ""
`other-instrument reference 004` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 3 'instrument maker'", 44, "the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", ""
`other-instrument reference 005` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 3 'legislative instrument'", 46, "the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", ""
`other-instrument reference 006` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 3 'penalty unit'", 48, "section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991", "Sentencing Act 1991", "section 110"
`other-instrument reference 007` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 3 'statutory rule'", 49, "the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", ""
`other-instrument reference 008` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 9(2)", 94, "Part 2 of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Part 2"
`other-instrument reference 009` MEANS `Reference to another instrument` OF "s 12", 127, "the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", "Subordinate Legislation Act 1994", ""

`the references to other instruments in the text` MEANS
    LIST `other-instrument reference 001`
       , `other-instrument reference 002`
       , `other-instrument reference 003`
       , `other-instrument reference 004`
       , `other-instrument reference 005`
       , `other-instrument reference 006`
       , `other-instrument reference 007`
       , `other-instrument reference 008`
       , `other-instrument reference 009`

-- A row resolves when the cited identifier is in the index and the row's heading is the index's heading for it.
GIVEN row IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cross-reference resolves` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision with the identifier` (row's `cited identifier`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `heading as printed` EQUALS row's `heading of the cited provision`
